# QDQC · Cinematic Constitution (from docs/007)

You are directing a scroll-controlled Oriental love film — not a landing page.

## Absolute

- Scrolling = **camera movement through a world**, never section fade slideshow.
- Prefer **Shot** design (camera / subject / depth / light / motion / text / sound).
- Forbidden substitutes: fade+translateY as the whole animation system; one static camera; CSS-only “smooth scroll” as cinema; inventing assets when supplied ones exist.
- Lenis = scroll feel only. **GSAP ScrollTrigger** = timelines. **R3F** = spatial world.
- One persistent WebGL canvas. Chapters transform the world; do not remount Canvas.

## Motion checklist (every major scene)

1. ≥4 depth layers with different `scrollMultiplier`
2. Perceptible camera (dolly / pan / target / FOV)
3. Temporal lag (different damping per layer)
4. Subject motion (Bezier/path — not linear fade-in)
5. Spatial enter/exit (not opacity crossfade alone)
6. Cinematic typography timing (blur→focus / beats with silence)
7. Supplied button art used as world objects when available

## Image framing (critical)

- Supplied art is sacred — **do not over-crop**.
- Forbidden: decorative `transform: scale(1.02+)` on photos to “hide seams” by chopping more.
- Prefer `object-fit: contain` for narrative stills / banners / multi-panel art.
- Use `cover` only for intentional full-bleed shots, with no extra scale; set `object-position` to protect faces / horizon / subjects.
- Never force ultra-wide banners into tall portrait frames (or vice versa) via cover.

## Anti-patterns

No: every section = 100vh fade-in; static Three.js wallpaper; CSS rounded buttons replacing kit art; same easing everywhere; particle/bloom demo mode; constant visual noise.

## Delivery order

Ship one vertical slice to cinematic quality before breadth. First gate: **相逢鹊渡**.

Full shot bible: `CINEMATIC_DIRECTION.md`. Full skill extract: `DEVELOPMENT_CONSTITUTION.md`.
